# GetJointInfo.srv — read-only robot-joint introspection for tooling.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
#   TrajectoryGoal.goalsets[i].target_joint_positions is a bare float list
#   that the node resolves VERBATIM in the robot config's cspace order
#   (`kinematics.cspace.joint_names`). A client that wants to plan in joint
#   space therefore has to know that order — and there was no way to ask for
#   it. The only place it leaked out was the /ik RESPONSE (its
#   `joint_states.name`), i.e. only as a side effect of paying for a GPU IK
#   solve. This service reports it directly, together with the position
#   limits a UI needs to bound its sliders, so an rviz joint-state panel can
#   be correct without guessing.
#
# READ-ONLY AND CHEAP
#   It touches no solver and rebuilds nothing: it only reads the already
#   parsed kinematics model. It is therefore safe to poll. A joint-lock
#   CHANGE (SetJointLocks) rebuilds the model and every solver (~20 s) — this
#   service does not, it just reports.
#
# AFTER set_joint_locks
#   `joint_names` is the cspace AFTER the change: a locked joint is dropped
#   from it (that is what "locked out of the cspace" means), and reappears
#   under `locked_joint_names` at the value it is pinned to.

# --- Request (empty: this is a pure query) ---
---

# --- Response ---
bool success
string message

# cspace order — exactly the order `target_joint_positions` expects, and the
# order of lower_limits/upper_limits. Empty only if the model has no cspace.
string[] joint_names

# Position limits, parallel to joint_names. math.inf (not 0) marks a joint the
# model reports no bound for, so a UI can leave that slider unbounded instead
# of clamping the user to a zero-width range.
float64[] lower_limits
float64[] upper_limits

# Joints currently pinned out of the cspace (the robot YAML's own
# `kinematics.lock_joints` unless a SetJointLocks override is in force),
# parallel to each other. Same values a read-only SetJointLocks query
# reports — repeated here so one call is enough to render the whole panel.
string[] locked_joint_names
float64[] locked_positions
